fork-p18 (Rapida ra-1okhu, ra-c2kyq.12, ra-4sj5g.1; founder approval
2026-10-30). Three additions, all render-only or read-only:

fork_version: FPDF_GetForkVersion() returns the fork release this library was
built from ("chromium/8076-fork-p18"), so an embedder can check at run time
which build it loaded. Each later fork patch bumps it.

annot_render_hide: FPDFAnnot_SetRenderHidden(document, annot, hidden) leaves
one annotation out of every render of the document (CPDF_AnnotList::DisplayPass)
and, for widgets and popups, from FPDF_FFLDraw (CPDFSDK_PageView::PageView_OnDraw)
while set, e.g. while the user drags it; a popup is hidden with its /Parent.
FPDFDoc_ClearRenderHiddenAnnots draws them all again. Held by the document handle only, keyed by the annotation
dictionary: never written to the file.

widget_oc_context: FPDF_FFLDraw built an optional-content context for the
render but CPDFSDK_PageView::PageView_OnDraw passed widgets only a bool, so
CPDF_Annot::DrawAppearance rendered their appearance streams with no OC context
and marked content in an OCG that is off (or turned off by the document's view
state) was drawn. The page view now holds the draw's render options while it
draws, and the widget's appearance is rendered with them. FFLCommon's OC
context now takes the Print usage under FPDF_PRINTING (it was always View,
which did not matter while widgets ignored it).

